  "summary_md": "A wave of portfolio reshaping and a bifurcated consumer credit cycle define today’s batch. Conglomerates are actively repositioning—AIRT vaulted its aviation asset management scale with the Crestone-Arena deal, while MATW’s arbitration win and battery-tech milestones cemented its pivot to higher-margin focus. In credit services, record origination volumes sit alongside rising delinquencies at the lower end of the borrower spectrum: CPSS scaled subprime auto lending profitably with AI-driven underwriting, yet OPFI and RM faced mounting charge-offs and credit stress that prompted an investor exit in OPFI. The acquisition exit for LPRO at a substantial premium and the transformative platform shift at GDOT further stand out, while insider conviction plays at TUSK and VRM underscore turnaround bets in capital-intensive niches.",
